    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The regulatory authority spent more than two years of proceedings under EU regulations, ultimately rejecting the affected entity's proposals. Now, European authorities are imposing a crushing financial blow in the high hundreds of millions of euros against Google's parent company for favoring its own services in search rankings, a continuation of past penalties that underscores the digital markets framework's reach.",
